Engine companion to sdl-engine's SDL/0053 ("dos: engine-signaled
pre-shutdown gate disable"). 5 functional LOC in SoundManager.cpp.

Mechanism. SDL/0050 ships a default-ON GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate
that gives +7 fps in steady-state gameplay (sdl_0050_ship_with_freeze.md)
but causes Quit-to-DOS to freeze the system: the SDL audio thread
holds `device->lock` during an `SDL_Delay(10)` inside the gate, and
the cooperative DOS scheduler never gives the main thread enough
runtime inside `SDL_LockMutex(device->lock)` (called from
`DestroyPhysicalAudioDevice` via `MIX_DestroyMixer`) to set the
shutdown atomic. SDL/0051's atomic-bypass at the top of GetDeviceBuf
is dead code for the same reason: main can't reach the line that
sets the atomic.

SDL/0053 exports `void SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown(void)` via the
workspace-local header `<SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h>`. The function
flips the same module-scope state variable that the SDL/0050 hint
killswitch (`SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE`) controls,
but from outside the audio thread's lock window. After the call,
the audio thread takes the fast default-path return on its next IRQ
wake (no SDL_Delay, no lock held); main acquires the lock within
~10 ms; teardown completes cleanly.

Engine companion. Add `#include <SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h>` to
SoundManager.cpp (unconditional; the header is safe on any host --
sdl-engine style-matched it to `SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h` which
also has no header-body platform guard; the symbol only exists in
`libSDL3.a` on DOS builds via `SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_DOS_SOUNDBLASTER`).
Insert the call between the existing `[3/6]: pre-Pixtone::shutdown`
and `[4/6]: pre-MIX_DestroyMixer` debug-log markers, with a new
`[3.5/6]` marker so the doskutsu_dbg_log trace shows the gate-disable
happened in the correct ordering relative to MIX_DestroyMixer.

Why call from SoundManager::shutdown(), not main.cpp engine-
shutdown. The contract requires the call to land AFTER all engine-
side audio producers have stopped (Pixtone::shutdown, Organya::
shutdown, MidiScheduler::shutdown -- all complete by the `[3/6]`
marker) but BEFORE MIX_DestroyMixer triggers SDL_audio.c's
DestroyPhysicalAudioDevice path. The SoundManager::shutdown body is
the only place that ordering is guaranteed and visible in one
function. Placement at engine-level `main.cpp` shutdown-[7/8] would
be wrong direction (audio thread already torn down by then).

The call is unconditional (no env-var gate). The engine-side does
not check whether SDL/0050's quiescence gate is currently ON or OFF
because (a) the gate is default-ON in production, (b) calling
`SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown` when the gate is already OFF is a cheap
state-flip no-op, (c) any gating would just add a fragile second
hint to keep in sync. The unconditional call is the simplest correct
behavior.

fps impact. Zero direct. This is purely a quit-cycle correctness
fix. Removes the freeze-on-quit known-issue #18 documented in
`sdl_0050_ship_with_freeze.md`. The SDL/0050 +7 fps gameplay gain
is preserved unchanged (the gate only disables during the
SoundManager::shutdown sequence; before that, every flip still
benefits from the quiescence skip).

Smoke. Builds clean at i486 -O3 -funroll-loops. New strings in
binary: `snd-shutdown[3.5/6]: SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown ...`
(SDLDBG.LOG bracket); `_SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown` symbol link
verified via nm; sdl-engine's audio-side `audio: SDL_DOSAudioBegin-
Shutdown` SDLDBG marker also pulled in. Existing slot 0128 markers
(TILE_BOUNDS_SKIP, thrashing-detect engaged) retained; slot 0127
Lever B markers still absent (wave-32 revert intact). Real-HW gate
is operator quitting cleanly from PLAY5 quit-cycle (no freeze, no
soft-reset required).

STOP-and-ack hygiene. None triggered. SDL/0053 header signature
(`void SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown(void)`) matches the spec from
sdl-engine's DM; nm verification on `libSDL3.a` confirms symbol
exported; SoundManager.cpp shutdown ordering matches the spec
(`[3/6]` and `[4/6]` markers at lines 740 + 745 respectively;
companion lands as `[3.5/6]`).
---
 src/sound/SoundManager.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
index fcf610d..3bea1e5 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,11 @@
 #include "SoundManager.h"
+// patch 0129 (Phase 11 wave-33): SDL/0053 companion. Header exports the
+// `SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown(void)` symbol that lets the engine pre-empt
+// the SDL/0050 quiescence gate before MIX_DestroyMixer reaches the
+// device->lock contention point. Workspace-local header (never
+// upstreamed); only defined on DOS builds via libSDL3.a's
+// SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_DOS_SOUNDBLASTER outer guard.
+#include <SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h>
 
 #include "../ResourceManager.h"
 #include "../common/misc.h"
@@ -740,6 +747,27 @@ void SoundManager::shutdown()
   doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[3/6]: pre-Pixtone::shutdown");
   Pixtone::getInstance()->shutdown();
 
+  // patch 0129 (Phase 11 wave-33): pre-empt SDL/0050's GetDeviceBuf
+  // quiescence gate so the audio thread takes the fast default-path
+  // return on its next wake. Without this signal, MIX_DestroyMixer below
+  // calls into SDL_audio.c's DestroyPhysicalAudioDevice which blocks on
+  // SDL_LockMutex(device->lock) -- but the audio thread holds that lock
+  // during a 10 ms SDL_Delay inside DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf's
+  // quiescence gate. Cooperative DOS scheduler never lets main acquire
+  // the lock long enough to set the atomic shutdown flag, so the lock
+  // contention is indefinite and the system freezes on Quit-to-DOS
+  // (iter L L1, iter M M1 2026-05-08; root cause in
+  // docs/PHASE11-ITER-M-FREEZE-DIAGNOSTIC.md sec. 18). Calling
+  // SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown here flips the gate state OUTSIDE the
+  // audio thread's lock window -- audio thread takes the fast return
+  // on next IRQ wake, lock releases within ~10 ms, main acquires it,
+  // teardown completes. The SDL/0050 fps gain (+7 fps) is preserved
+  // during gameplay; only the shutdown path bypasses the gate.
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[3.5/6]: SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown "
+                   "(flips SDL/0050 quiescence gate disable; avoids "
+                   "device->lock contention freeze)");
+  SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown();
+
   // DOS-PORT: SDL3_mixer's destroy is MIX_DestroyMixer(mixer); pairs with
   // MIX_CreateMixerDevice. MIX_Quit() then unwinds the global state.
   doskutsu_dbg_log("snd-shutdown[4/6]: pre-MIX_DestroyMixer "
